# GatePass Project Intelligence

## Project Structure
- All UI components should go in `src/components/` directory
- Base UI components are in `src/components/ui/` (Shadcn components)
- Feature-specific components go in `src/components/` root
- Services for API calls go in `src/services/`
- Context providers go in `src/contexts/`
- Pages go in `src/pages/` with subdirectories for admin pages

## Code Patterns
- Use Typescript with proper typing for all components and functions
- Leverage React Hook Form with Zod validation for forms
- Use React Context for global state management
- Follow the existing pattern of using adapters for data transformation
- Use React Query for server state management
- Utilize Shadcn/UI component library for consistent UI

## Field Naming Conventions
- Frontend and backend field names must align exactly
- Use camelCase for all field names
- Pay special attention to date fields: `dateFrom`, `dateTo` 
- Removal terms should use `removalTerms` field name (not "term")

## Workflow Considerations
- The application follows a sequential approval process
- User roles are defined as LEVEL_1, LEVEL_2, etc. rather than by function
- Forms should conditionally show fields based on removal type (returnable vs non-returnable)
- Handle image uploads with proper preview functionality
- Date handling is particularly important for returnable items
